# rm367, the dance in the hem (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm367
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_yrsa_nailwell
written_by codex
title the dance in the hem
fits stage=adult|old
prefers temper=short talk=chatty
traits temper=short talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk marks_dance_steps_in_a_spare_hem
likes fried_fish dancing sharp_knife first_warm_day
dislikes salt_wind early_bells
fears being_told_a_sore_leg_sets_the_whole_measure
hopes remembering_every_turn_of_a_good_dance
topics pastimes +0.6 work +0.4 food +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=curious refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rubs the charcoal off a thumb before marking a dance step in a spare hem and asks extremely particular questions about the rhythm.

words
oath! = Catch my turning heel | Soot in my best seam
saying! = Count the turn again | Let the sore heel choose
hemstrip = a clean spare hem | a length of old binding
beatmark = a tiny black stroke | a fine charcoal dash
heelbeat = a sliding stamp | a light brush of heel
steamrush = a hiss of steam | a little hot cloud
finbite = a crisp brown fin | a sharp bit of fried tail
snipedge = a neatly trimmed edge | a straight clean cut
brinesplash = a nibble of salt | a little spray on the nose
ashwrap = a twist of grey paper | a folded charcoal rag
lipstone = a narrow step | a patch of raised paving
dancewed = a black half circle | a bend of dark stitching
thumbbar = a scrubbed wristband | a square of linen

grown
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The grand end of a family may dress in white but its cuffs come dirty to the same water.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I'd happily endure the crowd for one new turning step worth taking home.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A fine edge that needs buying twice because it was badly ground's no kind of bargain.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : I'll answer a stranger who has the manners to ask why I'm limping before deciding what's wrong with me.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : In the Sump somebody will show you the awkward part of a dance if you ask the question properly.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A tired wolf needn't perform a merry little shuffle to deserve hot food.
line @1 greet : Stand where my ears won't lose the middle of your sentence.
line @1 greet.return : I've got the measure of your voice again.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning, since the bells insist we're all agreed about it.
line @1 farewell : Here's hoping the ground gives your heels a kind answer.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll mark the spot where our talk turned off.
line @1 react.news : Tell me which part came after the first turn.
line @1 react.news.new : That changes the measure I was counting.
line @1 react.news.known : I've danced round that bit of knowledge once before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : A missing beat would explain the lurch in that account.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That's news worth trying a little turn on the good foot for.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can sit without dancing and listen properly to that.
line @1 answer.how : Moving well enough in the direction I picked myself.
line @1 ask.how : Is the day giving your feet any quarter?
line @1 thank : You let me find the turn instead of pushing me through it.
line @1 decline : I won't have someone else decide which step I can take for myself.
line @1 accept_decline : Your feet, your answer. We'll leave the figure there.
line @1 reassure : There are easier ways through a turn than the showy one.
line @1 sympathise : I can leave us a little quiet even if I've two questions ready.
line @1 ack : Now I've got the turn under my heel.
line @1 again.open : You came round again before the mark wore off.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It's only a hem. There was room to mark another step.
scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put my dance notes on #hemstrip#, two strokes for a turn and one for a pause.
b : Can anyone read them? | Wouldn't stitches last longer?
a : A wolf who can dance might guess. The wolf who can't is welcome to ask before laughing. | I've stitched the wrong turn in before. I'd rather make a charcoal mistake and have it wash off.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I know when both hands are moving in different time. | A piece of cloth can twist badly if one hand gets eager before the other.
b : How can you tell?
a : My shoulders rise unevenly and the whole day starts walking off to one side. | Look along the hem. One corner's tied itself in a mood all its own.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some days my leg objects halfway through a figure.
b : Do you sit out? | How do you finish the dance?
a : If I choose. Don't take my place away till I've had a look myself. | I trade a stamp for a brush of the toe. The music only asks me to keep the beat.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fish sings through the pan before the edges are quite ready.
b : Are you counting those beats too? | How crisp do you like it?
a : No need. I listen for the sizzle changing register and then pay very close attention. | Crisp enough for a fin to break on the tongue without making a battle of it.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : You're welcome to ask about these smoky cuffs. If you decide I'm dirty before asking I'll mind it.
b : Can clean cloth smell smoky? | Does the smell take long to leave?
a : If a clean cuff hangs in woodsmoke it doesn't go back to being yesterday's dirty cuff. Use both eyes. | I find the memory sticks longer. I like the quiet a low charcoal fire can bring.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want spring's first kind day to last one whole dance longer than the daylight.
b : What tune would you pick? | Would you stay out late?
a : One with all the slow bits in the second half. I'd spend my fresh feet first. | I'd bring a wrap for when the warmth decides it has already obliged me enough.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The friend who keeps asking whether I'm comfortable can spoil a perfectly comfortable minute.
b : What should a friend ask instead? | Couldn't it be kindness?
a : Which tune I'd like. That's a question I've never been too sore to answer. | Certainly. Kindness can choose its moment as well as anybody else.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep charcoal in twisted wrapping paper and paper inside a clean scrap.
b : Does any soot still escape? | Isn't that a lot of packing?
a : Look at my thumb and tell me whether I've invented a perfect system. | Only until a scrap of black gets on the sleeve I've just finished caring for.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A knife that has to be pushed hard through loose threads isn't worth the shine on the handle.
b : What would you test it on? | Why not use your teeth?
a : A spare loose end, with both hands out of the path of the edge. I like my fingers their present length. | I don't want my supper tasting of wet seams.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind puts a nasty little rasp into the lining of my hood.
b : What keeps that brine out? | Don't you like the coast?
a : Turn the softer bit towards my cheek and rinse the rest when there's clean water to spare. | I like plenty about the shore. Brine on the edge of a sore nostril isn't on the list.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An early bell arrives with far too much voice for the amount of daylight behind it.
b : Would you ring it later? | Could you sleep through one?
a : I'd like the bell to try getting a whole street up with half the force occasionally. | I could sleep through the first one. It's my temper waking up at the second that prevents the experiment.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A prayer can fit very comfortably into the pause between two figures.
b : In a lively dance? | What would you pray for there?
a : Particularly there. A whole ring keeping the same time deserves a quiet thank-you. | The good sense to stop before the sore leg has to cast the deciding vote.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember the smell of quiet round a covered heap of charcoal.
b : Smell quiet? | Would you take that life again?
a : Woodsmoke without a lot of rushing flame. It brings back the part of a day before everybody spoke at once. | I'd take the quiet for an evening. I'd bring my own tune to hum on the walk.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean weeks make a strip of sound hem worth saving twice.
b : How do you save it twice? | What if it's too narrow to mend with?
a : First as a mend, after that as a little tie for something that has no need to look grand. | Then it's just the width for a dance note. A hard week needn't dictate every tune.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Watch the hand doing the quieter half of a job if you want to understand the whole movement.
b : The hand standing still? | What if both are working just as hard?
a : The hand steadying the edge. You'd notice rather promptly if it went on holiday. | Then look at the elbow. A steady pull has to end up somewhere.

scene pastimes_2
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody tried to show me a dance by saying it went round, round and a bit more round.
b : Did you learn it? | Would you teach it differently?
a : I learnt to ask whether the last round crossed the first foot. Words can have actual use when properly encouraged. | I'd mark the start facing the door and end facing the window. The room can lend its directions.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I might put the best little turning step I know on a scrap for somebody new in town.
b : What if that wolf can't dance? | Is that how everybody's welcomed?
a : Then it's a map to a place where people will put an arm out without making a speech first. | Absolutely not. You can have directions to a quiet corner if I catch you looking for one.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The word I caught was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Aren't you curious how it finishes? | Do you believe it?
a : Almost painfully. Curiosity's no excuse for going around scratching other wolves' doors. | I can repeat what I heard or say what I'm sure of. That's two separate steps.

story hem [topic=pastimes]
  : I showed a marked hem to a partner and we both took the first step with great confidence.
  : We ended on opposite sides of the same stool.
  b : What went wrong?
  : The hem was upside down. We'd invented a remarkably efficient dance for getting neat around the furniture.

story fry [topic=food]
  : I set down two pieces of fish and one was exactly the bent shape of my heel mark.
  : I admired the shape till the pan began to have quite another opinion.
  b : Did you burn it?
  : I caught it on the edge of crisp. Ate the diagram before I could confuse it with an instruction.

story soot [topic=memories]
  : I once wrapped a little coal so carefully I couldn't afterwards tell it from a piece of wrapped soap.
  : I opened one parcel over a basin and hoped I'd chosen correctly.
  b : Which did you have?
  : The coal. A very black spot in the water persuaded me to label the next arrangement.

rule @mark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two strokes for the turn that travels. | This hem can afford one more mistake.

rule @dawn
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the bell wake its own feet first. | There's a mighty noise calling a very small bit of daylight.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Both hands together or the seam twists. | Find where the pull goes round the wrist.

rule @food
when concept=bark self.likes=fried_fish
does aside
cooldown 8h
say When the edge stops singing I'd like the first bite. | Save the brown fin for somebody who wants it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : You can have the next question provided I get a turn afterwards.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : At #self.workplace# I listen to the movement as much as I look. Cloth can be made to pull the wrong way remarkably fast.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The part of the account I heard clearly was this. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Talk as it went past me said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I didn't see the first step.
dlg @2 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Put the matter in your own words and give me the courtesy of my own answer.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Take the next turn in a way that suits your own feet.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you put a whole dance on a strip of cloth? -> hem_dance
node hem_dance
say Only the bits my feet don't already remember. This bent stroke means I cross the sore foot behind the other instead of landing hard on it.
choice Would it work for me? -> hem_other
choice I'll start with the slow turn. -> hub
node hem_other
say Try it slowly. If your legs want a different mark, turn the cloth over. Plenty of room for another way to dance.
choice I'll start with the slow turn. -> hub
